WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
FormalSLT: machine-checked statistical learning in Lean.

00:05.000 --> 00:09.500
VC theory, Rademacher complexity, chaining,
PAC-Bayes, sequential inference, and dependent data.

00:09.500 --> 00:14.000
One stack connecting capacity, complexity,
selection, time, and dependence.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.500
VC growth bounds and metric entropy
feed complexity estimates.

00:18.500 --> 00:23.000
Those estimates lead to
finite-sample learning guarantees.

00:23.000 --> 00:27.500
PAC-Bayes prices posterior selection
with relative entropy.

00:27.500 --> 00:32.000
One event covers every posterior
allowed by the theorem.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.500
Confidence sequences and e-processes
remain valid under repeated looks.

00:36.500 --> 00:41.000
One event covers every time
and every declared choice.

00:41.000 --> 00:45.500
Choose from the observed prefix.
Fix the score before the next state.

00:45.500 --> 00:50.000
A Poisson correction connects path evidence
to stationary risk in the setting shown.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.500
One controlled-queue case study:
4,608 coordinates reduce to one hit rate.

00:54.500 --> 00:59.000
Hit-rate discrepancy equals row TV inside
the declared family; this is not a membership test.

00:59.000 --> 01:03.000
Checked anchors span VC ERM, metric entropy,
anytime PAC-Bayes, and adaptive trajectories.

01:03.000 --> 01:06.000
The queue is one application
of this wider library.

01:06.000 --> 01:12.164
FormalSLT: a Lean foundation for statistical learning
and modern finite-sample inference.
